From aeb5d7ca9a5f03a691c1d502e8e4ec3cc347bca2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 18:09:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 40/81] h713: standby phases, the kernel's net request and
 confirm, a clean reset

Until now a standby had no guard between the kernel's last word and
its first word after the wake: crust has no armed watchdog, a hang
anywhere stayed a hang, and a restart asleep waited in SS_OFF for a
second wake (PRUEFUNG5 CS-02, CS-08, F8, N-01). The release design
gives every phase one guard; drivers/hdmi/sun50i-h713-sleep.c keeps
them in the contract page's K block (SB_STATE, CYCLE, NET_ACC, NET_MS):

- PRESLEEP: 0x25/0x26 takes the kernel's NET_REQ (mark 0xa5, format 1,
  cycle CYCLE+1, phase OFF or RELEASED, both budgets set) before the
  answer goes out; budgets from NET_BUDGET, at most 120 s. Anything
  else sets error bit 12 and is not taken. NET_REQ 0 (the prepare
  round trip, a v4 kernel) changes nothing.
- CPU_OP at the cpu op req, SLEEP when the state machine suspends,
  RESUMING when CPU0 is released (or 0x11 without a sleep), RELEASED
  on NET_CONFIRM with the cycle. A cpu op req without a request (v4
  TF-A) sleeps as before and goes straight to RELEASED; CYCLE counts
  it.
- NET_MS counts the net phases from the tick timer, across restarts;
  PRESLEEP and RESUMING end in a clean reset when their budget is up.
- h713_restart_check() first thing in the state machine: a restart in
  CPU_OP, SLEEP or RESET resets; in PRESLEEP or RESUMING the state
  stays, the third restart there resets. A first start (diag starts 0)
  is not looked at.
- h713_fail(): cause, error bit, detail and data recorded, the R_PRCM
  sleep state this image can set undone (pad hold; LDO and VDD_SYS
  only in images with those steps), then the SoC watchdog with the
  feeding reset sequence - with H713_SLEEP_NET first the R_WDOG and
  after 2 s the SoC watchdog, FAIL_PATH says which. GP5 stays.

With H713_SLEEP_NET the R_WDOG is armed when the request is taken
(read back into NET_RB and SB_STATE bit 4), fed at step boundaries
(record_step) and at most once a second in the awake and asleep
loops, never inside a step, disarmed on the confirm; a first start
that finds it armed records it (NET_FOUND, error bit 15) and disarms
it. Without the net nothing touches the R_WDOG.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
